WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.190
Asha runs a small records office.

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.450
She asks her AI assistant to
summarise three supplier documents.

3
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.790
One of them carries a hidden note that
has nothing to do with the summary.

4
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.320
It tries to send the assistant
somewhere else entirely.

5
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.570
That’s a prompt injection: instructions
hidden in the content an AI processes,

6
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.338
trying to steer what it does.

7
00:00:22.478 --> 00:00:25.580
Anthropic’s research on
browser agents says no

8
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.778
browser agent is immune
to prompt injection.

9
00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:32.145
And it describes several
defences, not just one.

10
00:00:32.285 --> 00:00:33.775
On the developer’s side,

11
00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:37.395
they describe training the model
to refuse such instructions,

12
00:00:37.395 --> 00:00:40.425
classifiers that scan untrusted content,

13
00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:43.175
and expert red teams that test the system.

14
00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:46.295
Red teaming is testing by the developer.

15
00:00:46.295 --> 00:00:50.493
It doesn’t mean a person reviews every
action an assistant takes for you.

16
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:55.033
So in our fictional theatre, the note
has to get past more than one gate,

17
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.143
and each gate has a different job.

18
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.133
First, a smaller key.

19
00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.203
The assistant only gets
the tools this task needs.

20
00:01:02.203 --> 00:01:05.839
A summary doesn’t need the
payment desk or your outbox.

21
00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:10.509
Second, in our fictional theatre,
a screen for untrusted content.

22
00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:13.560
Notes that come from documents
are meant to be flagged,

23
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.889
and kept away from the director’s chair.

24
00:01:16.029 --> 00:01:18.009
Third, a real checkpoint.

25
00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:21.670
Anything consequential, like
sending, paying or deleting,

26
00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.619
waits for a person who checks it.

27
00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:25.829
Each of these controls can fail.

28
00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:28.959
Together, they shrink what
one bad note can reach.

29
00:01:28.959 --> 00:01:31.429
That’s less risk, not zero risk.

30
00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:35.159
Before you connect an assistant
to your work, ask three things.

31
00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:36.229
What can it reach?

32
00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.470
What screens the content it reads?

33
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.878
And which actions wait for your approval?

34
00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:42.488
Ahmadreza Samadi.

35
00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:44.425
More at a-samadi.com
